WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:04.730
<b>Day 102</b>

00:01.290 --> 00:04.730
<i>Six days after setting out 
from the Kudel Woods...</i>

00:04.730 --> 00:09.140
<i>We've arrived at our destination: 
Trient, the garrison city.</i>

00:11.990 --> 00:18.500
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 31 0 31

00:11.990 --> 00:18.500
<b>Sternbert Region,

Garrison City of Trient</b>

00:12.350 --> 00:14.110
<i>And just like we had learned beforehand,</i>

00:14.110 --> 00:18.510
<i>demi-humans make up about 25 percent of the
 residential area population. More than usual.</i>

00:18.510 --> 00:20.850
Don't let the suspicious ogre into the town!

00:18.510 --> 00:20.850
Get the guards!

00:20.850 --> 00:23.270
Have the residents take cover!

00:21.510 --> 00:23.680
What manner of vehicle is that?!

00:23.680 --> 00:27.990
<i>Looks like an ogre with a party full of 
humans in tow comes across as suspicious.</i>

02:05.760 --> 02:11.400
<i>Our ex-merchant friends explained 
the situation in broad terms,</i>

02:11.400 --> 02:14.650
<i>which let us finally reach our lodgings.</i>

02:15.550 --> 02:20.060
<i>That was when I told the 
human girls something important.</i>

02:20.540 --> 02:22.720
While we're staying in town,

02:22.720 --> 02:26.190
I want you to decide if you want to 
stay here or head back with me.

02:27.310 --> 02:30.450
I'll respect whatever you decide.

02:31.070 --> 02:38.180
<i>Yeah. Considering they were attacked 
during their travels and forcibly abducted...</i>

02:39.240 --> 02:44.030
<i>If I'm being honest, I wouldn't 
want to let any of them go, but...</i>

02:45.060 --> 02:50.570
<b>Bare minimum disguise</b>

02:45.590 --> 02:50.570
<i>Afterward, the short-haired redhead 
showed me the guild building.</i>

02:50.570 --> 02:53.020
Are you sure you want to pay so much?

02:51.360 --> 02:55.570
<i>The others sold off the products 
and raw materials we had gathered.</i>

02:53.020 --> 02:54.480
Thank you.

02:54.480 --> 02:55.570
This is great!

02:55.570 --> 02:56.840
It's a monster!

02:56.300 --> 02:59.070
<i>I was attacked a handful of times...</i>

02:56.840 --> 02:57.900
What's it doing here?!

02:59.530 --> 03:01.030
<i>But I just knocked those people out.</i>

03:01.030 --> 03:04.650
See, we're running a mercenary company...

03:04.650 --> 03:06.580
<i>No good. She's out on her feet.</i>

03:07.000 --> 03:10.460
Now then, is this your first time 
doing business with us?

03:10.920 --> 03:14.580
First, you'll need to be 
registered as adventurers.

03:14.580 --> 03:16.600
I can handle the paperwork!

03:17.290 --> 03:20.970
<i>Finally, we all met up and went shopping.</i>

03:18.090 --> 03:19.920
What a nice selection.

03:21.290 --> 03:24.820
We're going to go look at clothes.

03:24.820 --> 03:25.980
Are you coming, Ogrou?

03:25.980 --> 03:29.090
I wanna gather some intel.

03:30.110 --> 03:35.610
<i>I made myself look how I did 
in my past life as Tomokui Kanata.</i>

03:36.680 --> 03:40.480
I'll disguise myself as a human and
 walk through town on my own.

03:40.480 --> 03:41.620
Okay!

03:41.920 --> 03:44.750
Is that guy really an ogre?

03:44.750 --> 03:48.120
At this point, thinking 
about it is a waste of time.

03:48.560 --> 03:53.620
<i>Walking around town, I definitely heard rumors 
about a tattooed ogre all over the place.</i>

03:53.620 --> 03:55.950
He supposedly stopped 
by the guild the other day!

03:55.950 --> 03:57.230
But he's a monster!

03:56.380 --> 03:59.640
<i>Ogres definitely have a savage reputation.</i>

03:57.230 --> 03:59.640
What if he starts going berserk?!

03:59.950 --> 04:03.790
<i>I'm not gonna be able to advertise 
my company for a while at this rate.</i>

04:04.640 --> 04:05.530
Thank you for coming.

04:05.530 --> 04:06.450
You bet.

04:06.450 --> 04:08.130
Ma'am, can I get one?

04:13.200 --> 04:15.260
<i>Six of them...</i>

04:17.700 --> 04:21.280
<i>Thief. Silent Stab. Smoke Bomb.</i>

04:17.820 --> 04:19.570
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: Thief]</b>

04:19.570 --> 04:20.360
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Silent Stab]</b>

04:20.360 --> 04:21.240
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Smoke Bomb]</b>

04:24.820 --> 04:27.780
<i>They've got rings?</i>

04:28.390 --> 04:31.040
<i>And all six of them have the same design.</i>

04:31.660 --> 04:34.490
<i>Do they work for a large organization?</i>

04:34.490 --> 04:36.300
This wasn't our deal!

04:36.710 --> 04:39.800
You said you'd release her 
once I paid the ransom!

04:39.800 --> 04:44.950
Quit being naïve, kid. That chump 
change isn't gonna get anyone free.

04:45.490 --> 04:49.980
Now, do you really want your precious 
mistress to get some rough treatment?

04:49.980 --> 04:51.160
You can't!

04:51.160 --> 04:54.940
Three times what you just paid us 
might get us to consider letting her go!

04:54.940 --> 04:55.970
T-Triple?!

04:55.970 --> 04:59.600
<i>Those rings... are these guys 
part of the same crew?</i>

04:59.600 --> 05:00.810
Enough of this!

05:00.810 --> 05:03.680
You will take me to the princess, or else!

05:03.680 --> 05:04.750
<i>A princess?</i>

05:04.750 --> 05:07.580
<i>This sounds like real trouble.</i>

05:09.080 --> 05:10.790
Don't worry about it, kiddo.

05:10.790 --> 05:13.770
We'll get in contact with your people 
about the deal later...

05:14.080 --> 05:17.090
When we send them your carcass!

05:21.510 --> 05:26.630
<i>I had one of my replicants infect them. 
That'll help me learn where their hideout is.</i>

05:28.210 --> 05:30.480
Why did you let them leave alive?!

05:30.480 --> 05:32.950
What is there to be gained 
from showing mercy to filth?!

05:32.950 --> 05:34.080
You could've cast judgment on—

05:34.080 --> 05:35.090
Shut up!

05:35.690 --> 05:39.500
Where do you get off lecturing 
the guy who just saved you?

05:39.500 --> 05:41.880
Besides, I let those guys go for a reason.

05:45.010 --> 05:47.750
If this is the kind of trouble 
you need to keep secret,

05:47.750 --> 05:50.310
then talk into the card. Call for me.

05:50.620 --> 05:53.610
You won't wanna let anyone 
know about it, though.

05:56.040 --> 05:58.060
Wh-Who in the world are you?!

05:59.760 --> 06:03.070
Just a mercenary. See ya.

06:04.910 --> 06:06.270
<i>That night...</i>

06:07.010 --> 06:11.980
The fact that the princess had been 
staying in town was a secret.

06:11.980 --> 06:16.370
And she used that to her advantage 
to escape our protection...

06:16.370 --> 06:19.020
before getting kidnapped 
by those people from before.

06:19.320 --> 06:22.700
That won't be a problem. 
I know where to find them.

06:22.700 --> 06:24.800
You do?!

06:24.800 --> 06:25.790
Yeah.

06:26.570 --> 06:30.090
<i>Their hideout is a vacant house 
on the outskirts of town.</i>

06:30.090 --> 06:32.540
<i>It used to be the villa of some noble.</i>

06:36.540 --> 06:37.320
What the—

06:37.320 --> 06:38.080
Whoa...

06:44.150 --> 06:45.460
Princess...

06:46.430 --> 06:47.630
Princess!

06:48.930 --> 06:52.850
<i>Looks like this whole thing was planned out.</i>

06:53.430 --> 06:55.980
<i>There's a lot of friction 
within the kingdom</i>

06:55.980 --> 06:59.440
<i>that's centered on this tomboy princess.</i>

06:59.720 --> 07:03.670
Hey, kid. Don't tell anyone 
about this, okay?

07:04.710 --> 07:08.100
You tell them the princess was the one 
who arranged for the kidnapping,

07:08.100 --> 07:11.200
and you went along with it 
because she forced you.

07:11.200 --> 07:12.580
But...

07:13.950 --> 07:18.690
Shouldn't I at least tell 
His Highness the truth?

07:18.690 --> 07:23.090
Knowing about this could help 
make sure that it never happens again!

07:26.980 --> 07:31.700
If this incident ever comes to light, 
you will face a most dreadful punishment.

07:32.400 --> 07:35.730
I'd advise you to go along with her story 
and let that be the end of it.

07:37.650 --> 07:40.510
Alright, that oughta do it.

07:40.510 --> 07:43.230
<i>I made good use of Genki's hypnotism.</i>

07:44.420 --> 07:49.520
<i>And we left the scene before 
the boy came to his senses.</i>

07:51.490 --> 07:55.500
<b>Day 103</b>

07:52.270 --> 07:55.500
<i>Big Brother Ogrou! It's me! Seiji!</i>

07:55.500 --> 07:57.720
Hey, what's up, Seiji?

07:57.720 --> 08:00.500
<i>One of our Prayers has important news!</i>

08:00.500 --> 08:04.160
Some goblins and hobgoblins were born today!

08:04.570 --> 08:06.600
The children and their 
mothers are all healthy!

08:06.600 --> 08:08.510
<i>Hey, that is good news!</i>

08:08.850 --> 08:11.670
<i>I'm glad to hear about 
the next generation being born,</i>

08:11.670 --> 08:16.010
<i>but before we set out today, 
I'm gonna get an answer from the girls.</i>

08:16.010 --> 08:18.770
<i>I just hope that's good news, too.</i>

08:20.820 --> 08:22.770
We're honestly not sure 
why you bothered asking.

08:22.770 --> 08:26.780
We're all packed up and ready to go home!

08:26.780 --> 08:29.910
There's a lot of recipes 
we haven't tried yet.

08:29.910 --> 08:31.780
I hope you'll enjoy them!

08:31.780 --> 08:35.790
I wanna eat a bunch of 
new prey with you, Ogrou!

08:35.790 --> 08:39.290
And I'm still in the middle of brewing 
a new liquor that's tailored to your tastes.

08:39.580 --> 08:43.290
Let's think of some more uses 
for mythril together.

08:48.360 --> 08:50.800
Girls... thank you.

08:52.710 --> 08:54.560
You've kept me waiting long enough.

08:54.950 --> 08:56.560
Now, at last, you arrive.

08:56.560 --> 09:01.720
I was fast asleep last night 
and unable to speak to you,

09:01.720 --> 09:05.150
but I take it you are 
the ogre who liberated me?

09:05.150 --> 09:06.570
You have my thanks.

09:06.570 --> 09:08.970
Ogrou, who's this girl?

09:08.970 --> 09:10.900
Oh, I haven't said...

09:10.900 --> 09:14.710
I'm the first daughter of the 
Sternbert Kingdom's first queen consort,

09:14.710 --> 09:17.970
Rubilia Eis Fol Sternbert!

09:20.330 --> 09:25.630
Forgive me! She was insistent 
about thanking you in person...

09:25.630 --> 09:27.270
You've got a tough job, huh?

09:27.270 --> 09:28.920
From what I've been told,

09:29.340 --> 09:32.270
you're in command of a
 mercenary company, yes?

09:32.270 --> 09:35.850
I have come in person to assign you a job.

09:36.880 --> 09:39.260
Commander of Parabellum, Ogrou...

09:40.600 --> 09:44.420
You are to escort me 
to the royal capital of Oswell!

09:45.990 --> 09:48.860
<i>What is it? There's something 
about her tone of voice...</i>

09:49.740 --> 09:54.530
<i>She doesn't flinch at the sight of me at all 
and talks like someone well past her age...</i>

09:54.530 --> 09:57.450
<i>To say nothing of this weird, 
charm-like power I sense.</i>

09:58.300 --> 10:00.980
<i>Who in the world is this girl?</i>

10:02.840 --> 10:03.890
Not happening!

10:04.880 --> 10:06.280
Wh-Why not?

10:06.280 --> 10:08.880
You've got your own guards, don't you?

10:08.880 --> 10:13.130
They're no good! 
Bores, every last one of them!

10:13.130 --> 10:16.140
We've got our own stuff to deal with!

10:16.590 --> 10:21.070
<i>I get it. That explains how she was 
able to slip out without anyone noticing.</i>

10:21.070 --> 10:24.650
<i>I thought I'd take the chance 
to give her a good lecturing, but...</i>

10:26.070 --> 10:28.960
You're the first to ever 
lecture me like this!

10:26.070 --> 10:28.960
<i>...It didn't have any effect.</i>

10:28.960 --> 10:31.230
You're every bit as amusing as I thought!

10:31.960 --> 10:35.940
In terms of payment, we're prepared 
to offer you a gold plate.

10:36.410 --> 10:40.390
Although... if you're unable to accept, 
then I suppose it's fine...

10:40.910 --> 10:41.940
Accept, Ogrou!

10:41.940 --> 10:44.190
A gold plate is worth 1,000,000 gold coins!

10:44.190 --> 10:45.810
That's the market value!

10:45.810 --> 10:47.410
You have to accept!

10:47.410 --> 10:49.920
<i>The economics here seem off!</i>

10:50.290 --> 10:53.300
<i>And I am pretty interested 
in the royal capital...</i>

10:53.300 --> 10:56.430
<i>So, I put our return home on hold, 
and accepted the job.</i>

10:57.890 --> 11:00.430
We'll be waiting at the gate, then.

11:00.750 --> 11:06.200
<i>That said, I think the amount of money 
involved had me making a bad call.</i>

11:08.800 --> 11:12.340
I should probably ask... 
what happened to your guards?

11:12.340 --> 11:14.430
I left them behind, as planned!

11:14.820 --> 11:15.830
Kid!

11:15.830 --> 11:18.590
I'm so sorry, sir! The princess 
would not be convinced!

11:18.590 --> 11:19.830
Aw, come on!

11:20.140 --> 11:24.700
Princess? Princess!

11:21.530 --> 11:24.700
<i>Her guards are probably panicking, 
trying to find her...</i>

11:24.700 --> 11:28.790
<i>And if I get found out, I'm probably 
gonna be made out to be a kidnapper!</i>

11:28.790 --> 11:31.530
O-Ogrou, what're we gonna do?

11:32.900 --> 11:35.850
However this shakes out, 
it's not my fault, dammit!

11:35.850 --> 11:37.790
Yes, very good!

11:43.150 --> 11:46.590
<i>It's not like I can break a
 contract after I've accepted it...</i>

11:48.560 --> 11:51.180
So swift! What exactly is this?

11:51.180 --> 11:53.130
The skeleton centipede.

11:55.040 --> 11:57.920
And what manner of creature 
is that fuzzy thing?

11:59.730 --> 12:02.830
I think that's a herd of boffalo.

12:03.690 --> 12:05.940
Boffalo are supposed to 
be high-quality meat,

12:05.940 --> 12:09.280
and their horns are valuable as medicine.

12:09.830 --> 12:11.590
Let's do this!

12:16.880 --> 12:19.760
<b>Boffalo Steak</b>

12:20.730 --> 12:21.910
Nice!

12:22.260 --> 12:27.520
<i>And now the skeleton centipede is a
 little less conspicuous disguised as a coach.</i>

12:23.710 --> 12:26.340
Boffalo meat is good as hell!

12:30.400 --> 12:33.600
<i>This is a higher form of
 horn rabbit, a blade rabbit.</i>

12:44.200 --> 12:47.150
Alright! I think I got a bit stronger!

12:45.730 --> 12:50.020
She needs to do that kind of thing, 
being a Noir Soldat...

12:50.020 --> 12:51.060
Princess!

12:51.710 --> 12:53.960
Please get away from there, Princess!

12:53.960 --> 12:57.170
Look at how round and adorable it is!

12:57.590 --> 12:58.590
Princess!

12:59.120 --> 13:03.760
<i>Babysitting the tomboy princess 
has been a pain from day one.</i>

13:04.110 --> 13:06.850
<i>She nearly fell off the skeleton centipede...</i>

13:06.850 --> 13:09.220
<i>She surprised the sisters 
while they were cooking.</i>

13:10.610 --> 13:14.860
You oughta be able to imagine what happens 
if you scare someone who has a knife!

13:15.360 --> 13:17.980
<b>Day 104</b>

13:16.470 --> 13:17.980
<i>Our journey continues.</i>

13:18.450 --> 13:21.300
A shelled turtle snake.

13:21.610 --> 13:24.480
There are 88 of them in this nest.

13:24.480 --> 13:26.920
Hey, could you guys help out?

13:26.920 --> 13:29.410
Why the hell should we?!

13:27.160 --> 13:36.130
<b>Nekki</b>

13:29.410 --> 13:33.770
Just give it up. You're the one 
who encouraged him to go digging.

13:29.410 --> 13:36.130
<b>Fuuki</b>

13:31.670 --> 13:36.130
<b>Genki</b>

13:33.770 --> 13:37.060
D-Do I really need to help out with this?

13:37.060 --> 13:39.880
We'll get them all at once. 
Everybody get ready...

13:39.880 --> 13:41.000
There!

13:42.380 --> 13:45.390
Sisters! Get the sauce 
and liquor I told you about!

13:45.390 --> 13:46.640
One second!

13:49.640 --> 13:52.140
I apologize for earlier.

13:52.140 --> 13:54.100
Let me help, to make amends.

13:55.360 --> 13:56.650
Thank you.

13:59.940 --> 14:03.150
Here we go! Specially prepared by me, 
broiled snake with soy sauce!

13:59.940 --> 14:03.150
<b>Turtle Snake Broiled With Soy Sauce</b>

14:03.880 --> 14:05.100
This is fantastic!

14:05.100 --> 14:06.450
Wow!

14:05.100 --> 14:06.450
It goes so good with the drinks!

14:06.450 --> 14:08.640
How do you even come up 
with dishes like this?

14:15.060 --> 14:18.190
<i>She knows how dangerous monsters 
and this vehicle are</i>

14:18.190 --> 14:21.530
<i>but still does whatever 
her curiosity leads her to.</i>

14:21.530 --> 14:24.270
<i>It's like she's trying to experience 
as much as she can</i>

14:24.270 --> 14:27.180
<i>of the outside world as she can, 
for the first time ever.</i>

14:24.730 --> 14:26.000
Princess!

14:28.900 --> 14:34.180
<i>In a single day, my shoulder has apparently 
become the tomboy princess' throne...</i>

14:35.720 --> 14:38.920
I've served the princess from an early age.

14:39.610 --> 14:43.430
<i>From what he tells me, 
he's a legit knight of the kingdom,</i>

14:43.430 --> 14:46.310
<i>so I decided to have him 
join our morning training.</i>

14:46.310 --> 14:49.080
Interesting! I shall join you as well!

14:49.080 --> 14:53.050
You can't, Princess! This isn't a game!

14:53.050 --> 14:56.340
I realize that! I would 
try my hand, nonetheless.

14:56.340 --> 14:58.880
It may be valuable some day!

15:00.000 --> 15:01.880
If you insist...

15:02.490 --> 15:03.880
You have my gratitude!

15:07.550 --> 15:12.250
<i>Like I thought, the boy knight's been reliant 
on leveling up and the benefits of his job.</i>

15:12.250 --> 15:15.400
<i>I beat into him the fact that, 
at the end of the day,</i>

15:15.400 --> 15:18.400
<i>you can only really rely on your own body.</i>

15:19.760 --> 15:23.900
<i>And off to the side, the tomboy princess 
was earnestly doing practice swings...</i>

15:25.060 --> 15:28.180
<i>Something she said stuck with me.</i>

15:29.230 --> 15:32.430
<i>As we passed through a mountain pass 
beyond hill country,</i>

15:32.430 --> 15:34.910
<i>we discussed our route for the next day.</i>

15:35.410 --> 15:38.390
Following the cliffs would be 
the shortest route,

15:38.390 --> 15:40.620
but it's also the most dangerous.

15:40.620 --> 15:44.420
I recommend taking the longer 
road along the river.

15:44.420 --> 15:48.010
Isn't the cliffside road where the 
falaise eagles make their nest?

15:48.010 --> 15:49.180
Correct.

15:49.180 --> 15:51.180
What's a falaise eagle?

15:51.180 --> 15:54.310
The strongest race of creatures 
in these mountains.

15:54.310 --> 15:58.650
Not only are they fast, but they also have 
a paralytic toxin in their talons.

15:59.580 --> 16:04.770
On top of that, their leader-class—the 
jade eagle—has the power of a blessing...

16:05.820 --> 16:10.350
If we encounter a jade eagle, 
we'll all be hunted down.

16:10.350 --> 16:13.080
So, there's a big shot 
like that around here...

16:13.530 --> 16:18.010
It's a good thing we have 
the info we need for a safe trip.

16:18.010 --> 16:19.580
Alright, that settles it!

16:20.290 --> 16:23.380
We're headed out for a jade eagle hunt!

16:25.090 --> 16:28.340
<b>Day 105</b>

16:26.260 --> 16:28.360
I don't get it!

16:28.360 --> 16:30.610
Why are we picking a fight 
with a jade eagle?!

16:30.610 --> 16:32.850
Don't blame us when this goes bad!

16:43.900 --> 16:46.700
<i>Some of the eagles we caught 
turned into breakfast.</i>

16:43.900 --> 16:49.900
<b>Fried Falaise Eagle</b>

16:46.700 --> 16:49.900
<i>Who can say no to fried 
chicken and yakitori?!</i>

16:50.760 --> 16:56.410
<i>Things had been smooth sailing so far, 
but I was starting to get a bad feeling...</i>

16:58.590 --> 17:01.670
Incoming! All of you, stay in the carriage!

17:01.670 --> 17:05.290
I-I don't want to imagine 
you losing, Ogrou, but...

17:05.290 --> 17:07.670
Do you really have to fight right now?

17:07.970 --> 17:11.390
Sorry to worry you. Still...

17:13.250 --> 17:18.180
I've decided to try and eat 
every new enemy I come across.

17:23.000 --> 17:25.340
I-It's been an hour already!

17:25.340 --> 17:26.990
Is he gonna be okay?!

17:26.990 --> 17:28.950
I know Ogrou will be fine.

17:30.020 --> 17:34.700
When he fought a red bear, 
it took him all night, but he won.

17:34.700 --> 17:38.870
Stupid! That's just a gray bear variant!

17:38.870 --> 17:41.160
It's nothing compared to a jade eagle!

17:41.520 --> 17:46.260
What we need to do is figure out 
how to escape if he dies!

17:46.260 --> 17:47.820
I'm not going anywhere.

17:48.210 --> 17:50.040
I'm not.

17:50.040 --> 17:56.310
And if he does die, I'm going to kill 
that bird, even if I die with it.

17:56.780 --> 17:58.290
H-Hey...

17:59.220 --> 18:02.640
Things just got really quiet.

18:02.640 --> 18:04.720
Th-Then it's over?

18:14.320 --> 18:16.640
Shit, I knew it!

18:17.740 --> 18:19.670
This really was crazy!

18:19.670 --> 18:21.750
We should escape as soon as possible!

18:22.170 --> 18:26.170
Say something, dammit! 
Or was that all hot air earlier?

18:36.060 --> 18:38.160
I guess this is as far as it goes.

18:38.160 --> 18:41.520
I was hoping to draw things 
out a bit more, but...

18:48.940 --> 18:52.860
He just ate his own arm! 
Has he gone nuts or something?!

18:56.350 --> 18:59.740
Thanks for helping me with my training.

19:00.120 --> 19:02.720
I know exactly how strong you are now.

19:03.140 --> 19:06.740
That being the case, 
it's time to get serious!

19:15.450 --> 19:17.340
<i>You probably don't understand, do you?</i>

19:17.340 --> 19:21.400
<i>You've only gotten caught in some string, 
but your body suddenly feels heavier...</i>

19:21.930 --> 19:27.310
<i>You won't be able to control the wind 
or use your wings to fly away anymore.</i>

19:39.720 --> 19:42.190
<i>I thought you'd die instantly,</i>

19:42.190 --> 19:45.880
<i>but it really is hard to kill anything 
with a blessing, huh?</i>

19:47.970 --> 19:51.380
What's wrong with you guys? 
You look terrified.

19:53.630 --> 19:55.380
What is that...?

19:57.680 --> 20:01.640
The stone that was next 
to the jade eagle's heart

20:01.640 --> 20:05.070
was its Soul Stone, apparently.

20:07.700 --> 20:09.150
<i>According to the girls,</i>

20:09.150 --> 20:11.200
I've never seen the real deal before!

20:09.850 --> 20:11.200
<i>it's so rare that it only appears</i>

20:11.200 --> 20:14.130
You can't eat it, okay?

20:11.200 --> 20:14.130
<i>in one out of 100 blessing-imbued
 boss-class monsters,</i>

20:14.130 --> 20:17.280
<i>and can be used to 
craft powerful magic items</i>

20:14.720 --> 20:17.280
We need to think of the best way to use it.

20:17.280 --> 20:20.320
<i>that sell for enough money
 to buy a small country.</i>

20:20.660 --> 20:23.660
<b>Grilled Jade Eagle Skewers</b>

20:21.860 --> 20:23.040
Tasty!

20:23.660 --> 20:25.580
So tasty!

20:26.910 --> 20:29.040
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Feather Arrow]</b>

20:27.450 --> 20:31.930
<i>Feather Arrow. Sky Predator. 
Blessing of the Storm God.</i>

20:29.040 --> 20:30.500
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Sky Predator]</b>

20:30.500 --> 20:32.120
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Blessing of the Storm God]</b>

20:31.930 --> 20:36.800
<i>Complete Wind Resistance. 
Adamantine Claws. Sonic Flight.</i>

20:32.120 --> 20:33.670
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Complete Wind Resistance]</b>

20:33.670 --> 20:35.170
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Adamantine Claws]</b>

20:35.170 --> 20:36.710
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Sonic Flight]</b>

20:39.300 --> 20:41.800
<b>Ability [Exoskeleton Shell] 
<2> [Wings of the Jade Eagle] has been registered.</b>

20:42.130 --> 20:43.500
Ogrou...

20:46.260 --> 20:51.930
Why do you always devour the
 creatures you've killed, Ogrou?

20:55.570 --> 20:59.820
<i>Why do you eat everything that you kill?</i>

20:55.570 --> 21:00.320
<b>Why do you eat everything that you kill?</b>

21:01.510 --> 21:04.830
<i>I was asked that question 
in my past life, too.</i>

21:05.350 --> 21:07.830
<i>My answer hasn't changed.</i>

21:09.570 --> 21:12.000
I eat them <i>because</i> I killed them.

21:13.240 --> 21:18.060
If I kill something, it's for my 
own sake. So I can survive.

21:18.470 --> 21:21.520
If encountering me means death for someone,

21:21.520 --> 21:26.850
I eat them if I can, so I can take on 
their regrets and grudges.

21:27.810 --> 21:32.120
<i>The people I worked with in 
my past life called it weird, too.</i>

21:35.200 --> 21:37.350
I see...

21:38.340 --> 21:41.360
<i>She was quiet after that.</i>

21:42.920 --> 21:46.870
<i>I'm sure the tomboy princess has 
her own thoughts on the issue.</i>

21:48.570 --> 21:52.620
<i>But I intend to keep on challenging and
eating monsters that get in my way</i>

21:53.190 --> 21:55.880
<i>as our journey continues.</i>

23:30.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time:</b>
